{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02613",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Hello, come in. Mind the step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 4.6,
      "end_seconds": 8.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.59,
      "end_seconds": 15.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. Busy day out there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.04,
      "end_seconds": 21.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I mean, always is. The traffic coming in was terrible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.29,
      "end_seconds": 25.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.76,
      "end_seconds": 31.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a sudden painful cold leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.89,
      "end_seconds": 35.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.43,
      "end_seconds": 39.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Around about a month, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 40.62,
      "end_seconds": 44.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "hm, I'd say more like about two months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.07,
      "end_seconds": 51.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.5,
      "end_seconds": 56.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Uh, uh, I suppose so, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.22,
      "end_seconds": 64.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.85,
      "end_seconds": 68.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "it happens a few times a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.39,
      "end_seconds": 72.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.78,
      "end_seconds": 95.84,
      "duration_seconds": 18.06,
      "text": "It, It usually comes with not being able to move the foot. Oh, and numbness in the foot. That's been about the same, three weeks. The not being able to move the foot? That's been for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.75,
      "end_seconds": 113.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "So, a few quick ones: fever, chest pain or recent injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.45,
      "end_seconds": 117.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "No, nothing to to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.9,
      "end_seconds": 120.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.13,
      "end_seconds": 123.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.08,
      "end_seconds": 126.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.36,
      "end_seconds": 131.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.08,
      "end_seconds": 144.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.3,
      "end_seconds": 153.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Yes, diclofenac. I get swelling of my lips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.43,
      "end_seconds": 158.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.44,
      "end_seconds": 161.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.51,
      "end_seconds": 163.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.12,
      "end_seconds": 169.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I have acid reflux, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.62,
      "end_seconds": 181.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Right, so an irregular heartbeat is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.93,
      "end_seconds": 193.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.3,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.08,
      "end_seconds": 197.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.3,
      "end_seconds": 202.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 203.28,
      "end_seconds": 213.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the metoprolol was 100 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.39,
      "end_seconds": 218.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.13,
      "end_seconds": 226.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. I take omeprazole, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.43,
      "end_seconds": 230.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.38,
      "end_seconds": 232.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "20 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.91,
      "end_seconds": 237.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Right, did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.1,
      "end_seconds": 245.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Just my appendix taken out, when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.44,
      "end_seconds": 249.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.67,
      "end_seconds": 265.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Alright, bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.72,
      "end_seconds": 292.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "okay: temperature 36.7, blood pressure 133 over 76, SpO2 99 percent on room air, heart rate 122."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.67,
      "end_seconds": 296.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.36,
      "end_seconds": 299.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.13,
      "end_seconds": 302.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.3,
      "end_seconds": 321.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "The right leg is cold, pale and mottled, with no pulses at the groin or below."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.43,
      "end_seconds": 337.39,
      "duration_seconds": 13.96,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with an acutely ischaemic leg at this stage. I can't rule out a deep vein thrombosis yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.76,
      "end_seconds": 340.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.99,
      "end_seconds": 349.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an acutely ischaemic leg do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.12,
      "end_seconds": 396.91,
      "duration_seconds": 28.79,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an urgent CT angiogram for acute limb ischaemia. Let's use heparin, 5000 units, bolus now, single dose. That's for limb ischaemia. You need the vascular surgeons now, this is time critical. I think the vascular team should see you too. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. I'll want another look straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.28,
      "end_seconds": 404.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.49,
      "end_seconds": 410.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "good, thanks, I'll see you then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.68,
      "end_seconds": 412.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}